			"Message": "chore(Project): Sync Cocoon and Sky submodules\n\nUpdate Cocoon to d3408e6f8ffafedcf209a780133a8176bf0d9972 and Sky to b8a380955bb3217237de5df8129e2cadee710b52, bringing in the latest downstream improvements.\n\nThis synchronization pulls in recent changes from both component repositories.",
			"SHA": "faf66cd74f2ea263dedc12d8f1cafa7a410d6a7e"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T04:22:01Z",
			"File": [
				"⡿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				5
			],
			"Message": "feat(Project): Add terminal output buffering for late-listener replay\n\nMulti-component synchronization solving the same race condition that was fixed for tree-views and SCM:\n\n1. **Mountain**: Add per-terminal output buffering - `AppendTerminalOutput()` captures PTY bytes into a 64KB bounded buffer (keeps most recent suffix to preserve the prompt), `DrainTerminalOutputBuffer()` retrieves buffered data, `RemoveTerminalOutputBuffer()` cleans up on exit. Extend `sky:replay-events` to emit `sky://terminal/create` for each active terminal AND replay any buffered `sky://terminal/data` bytes.\n\n2. **Sky**: Extend replay-events log with terminal visibility - Add `terminals?: number` and `terminalDataBytes?: number` to the type definition and include them in the log summary alongside tree-views, SCM providers, and commands. This provides visibility into terminal sessions active during early boot when extensions may create terminals before the frontend is ready.\n\nThe PTY reader task and SkyBridge's `listen(\"sky://terminal/*\")` installation race: in bundled-electron profile, the shell's first prompt fires ~50ms after `spawn_command` while Sky's bundle still parses for ~1500ms. Without buffering, zsh MOTD, direnv exports, fish greetings are silently dropped.\n\nImpact: Terminal output is now preserved and replayed for late listeners, completing the replay system for all three major feature areas: tree-views, SCM providers, and terminals.",
			"SHA": "f7bd709946d39df256b3b6eedbb0e64dece31154"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T04:01:56Z",
			"File": [
				"⡿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				5
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Project): Sync submodules with SCM identifier, command replay, and retry logic\n\nMulti-component synchronization enabling multi-SCM support and improving boot reliability:\n\n1. **Common**: Add Identifier field to SourceControlManagementProviderDTO - enables provider identification (\"git\", \"github\", \"hg\") for multi-SCM support, maps to `scmId` in sky://scm/register events.\n\n2. **Mountain**: Use actual SCM provider identifier in replay instead of hardcoded \"git\", add command registration replay for extension-registered commands, reduce tree-view timeout from 5000ms to 1500ms for graceful failure.\n\n3. **Output**: Mirror retry logic on user extensions scan path (was missing), switch to exponential backoff (100-200-400-800-1500ms), short-circuit Promise protocol probes to eliminate spurious \"Unknown IPC command\" errors.\n\n4. **Sky**: Display commands count in replay-events log for visibility into early-boot command replay.\n\nImpact: Multi-SCM providers (github, hg) now replay correctly. User extensions load at boot even when Mountain scan is slow. Promise probes reduced from ~25ms to <1ms per wake cycle.",
			"SHA": "b15e1d818609f1ab74584410abb5c73f3628d9bf"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T03:40:55Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠇⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				8
			],
			"Message": "fix(Project): Sync submodules with sidebar fix and extension scan improvements\n\nMulti-component synchronization addressing Activity Bar emptiness and extension loading:\n\n1. Mountain: Add Sky event replay on listener registration - Mountain emits events before Sky listeners install, causing dropped `sky://tree-view/create` and `sky://scm/register` events. New `sky:replay-events` handler iterates active TreeViews and SCM providers to re-emit. Also adds path security checks and SCM provider emit failure logging.\n\n2. Output: Add retry logic to user extension scan path - User extension paths lacked the retry logic that system paths had, causing silent 0-extension responses. Add exponential backoff (100-200-400-800-1500ms) for async disk scans.\n\n3. Sky: Fix Rollup no-external dropping VS Code contribution imports - Activity Bar came up empty because Rollup was dropping side-effect imports (`extensions.contribution`, `scm.contribution`, `files.contribution`, `*.viewlet.js`...). Add normalized path matching for disk paths, package specs, and lowercase variants.\n\n4. Cocoon: Refactor code structure for improved readability and maintainability.\n\nImpact: Activity Bar now populates with extension-contributed views (GitLens, jsdebug, SCM providers). User extensions load properly at boot even when Mountain's async scan hasn't completed.",
			"SHA": "972a110b4e940290d87a1a0af952d93f16b42318"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T02:13:47Z",
			"File": [
				"⡟⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				4
			],
			"Message": "fix(Project): Fix circuit breaker trips from URI parsing and service isolation\n\nMulti-component synchronization preventing silent error cascades:\n\n1. **Mountain**: Fix false circuit breaker trips from URI parsing edge cases - Extensions frequently register watchers on optional paths (e.g., `~/.roo/skills-*`, `.vscode/settings.json` in fresh workspaces) that don't exist. Mountain now catches benign \"path not found\" errors and records a deferred entry. Additionally, Cocoon sends URIs in three formats (plain strings, objects with `external` field, legacy `scheme`+`path` objects), but only the `external` field was accepted, causing `Diagnostic.Set` to trip the breaker after 5 publishes, silencing all linters.\n\n2. **Output**: Fix ExposeWorkbenchAccessor transform silently failing - The import marker used single quotes but esbuild rewrites to double quotes post-bundle, causing the entire `__CEL_SERVICES__` patch to no-op (all SkyBridge hooks offline). Also wraps each `invokeFunction` in its own try-IIFE so a single missing service doesn't throw the entire facade undefined.\n\nImpact: File watchers no longer fail on fresh workspaces. Language extension diagnostics now publish without triggering circuit breaker. All SkyBridge services (search, SCM, status bar, tree views) now initialize correctly.",
			"SHA": "7cc10566bad81808c5008aaa95a040fb6b3c133f"
		}
	],
	"TimeStamp": 1778420673905
}